  "answer": "The study found one confirmed challenging case, not five. That case is scene 023b7fcc with the lead car shifted 1.0 s later, slowed to 0.75x, and 200 ms planner delay: every run there failed, and the range puts its failure rate surely above 0.5. These failures are not the clean rear-ends the brief asks about. The triage says that on this scene the policy steered out of its lane against the route command, then either clipped the lead car (actor 12) from behind or sideswiped a car in the next lane (actor 56). All of those failures were the policy's fault, and none are flagged as possible simulator artifacts. No other scene failed at any setting tried, and three of them clearly passed when repeated. So within the brief's knob ranges, this study found only one scene where retiming the lead car makes VaVAM fail.",
